red as nonblocking corroboration only; asking for it as a blocker would manufacture an objection beyond the observed evidence. Because a sufficient verdict requires empty requested_checks and contradictions, and the candidate still carries the E-002/E-003 mismatch and no observed cause-specific discriminator, the verdict is insufficient and the review abstains.\"}], \"decisions\": [{\"action\": \"INVESTIGATE\", \"reason\": \"Round 0: no findings, evidence, hypotheses, or candidate assessments exist yet in the incident_1003 observation window (started 2026-10-01T12:00:00Z) spanning gateway, backend, postgres, redis, payment. No causal mechanism is observable, so I must open discriminating evidence sources before any hypothesis can be justified. Budget is ample (remaining_tool_calls 32, affordable_tasks 23), so I dispatch one logs task and one changes task to establish error chronology and configuration/deployment diffs; these are the two most decisive independent sources and avoid premature symptom attribution.\", \"assignments\": [{\"task_id\": \"task-0001\", \"role\": \"logs\", \"question\": \"What error and warning log signatures appear for gateway, backend, and payment during the incident window, and in what chronological order do they first occur?\", \"allowed_tools\": [\"query_logs\"], \"filters\": {\"service\": \"backend\", \"severity\": \"ERROR\", \"start_ts\": \"2026-10-01T12:00:00Z\", \"end_ts\": \"2026-10-01T13:00:00Z\", \"limit\": 50}, \"reason\": \"No findings exist; first establish which service emits the earliest error and whether errors originate locally or are downstream of another dependency.\", \"expected_discriminator\": \"The earliest service to emit an error and its error signature distinguishes a locally-originating failure from a downstream symptom propagated from another service.\"}, {\"task_id\": \"task-0002\", \"role\": \"changes\", \"question\": \"Were there any deployment, config, maintenance, or scaling changes affecting gateway, backend