local saturation from database-induced latency. Budget is ample (remaining_rounds 7, remaining_tool_calls 28, affordable_tasks 20, minimum_requests_per_investigation 2), so I dispatch exactly the two blocking discriminators and reserve the remaining calls for review and the final decision. No new findings or evidence were produced since round 0, so hypothesis assessments are unchanged and no updates are emitted.\", \"assignments\": [{\"task_id\": \"task-0003\", \"role\": \"metrics\", \"question\": \"What do backend-scoped resource and latency metrics (request concurrency, worker/thread pool saturation, CPU and memory utilization, in-flight or queued requests, and request duration) show between 2026-10-01T12:00:00Z and 2026-10-01T13:00:00Z, and does any local saturation signal begin before or coincide with the backend deadline exceed at 2026-10-01T12:00:14Z?\", \"allowed_tools\": [\"query_metrics\"], \"filters\": {\"service\": \"backend\", \"start_ts\": \"2026-10-01T12:00:00Z\", \"end_ts\": \"2026-10-01T13:00:00Z\", \"metric_names\": [\"request_concurrency\", \"worker_pool_utilization\", \"cpu_utilization\", \"memory_utilization\", \"request_duration_p95\", \"inflight_requests\"]}, \"reason\": \"The backend_resource_saturation candidate has no observed internal mechanism: only one backing log record (incident_1003-E-003) exists and no backend-internal telemetry was ever fetched, so local saturation versus dependency-induced latency cannot be separated from the supplied records. This is the blocking causal source for the selected candidate and was explicitly requested by review.\", \"expected_discriminator\": \"Rising backend concurrency, worker/thread pool utilization, or CPU/memory pressure that predates the 12:00:14Z deadline exceed supports local resource saturation, whereas flat backend resource metrics with backend latency tracking an external dependency instead indicates a propagated dependency failure.\"}, {\"task_id\": \"task-0004\", \"role\": \"database\", \